WEBVTT

00:07:57.806 --> 00:08:01.769
And, you know, the last two years
have been of focus.

00:08:01.769 --> 00:08:05.523
They’ve been ... concerned.

00:08:05.981 --> 00:08:07.191
I have to say,

00:08:07.233 --> 00:08:10.694
I would love to just thank
all of my colleagues here at WHO.

00:08:10.736 --> 00:08:14.448
I mean, I work with incredible people
all over the world,

00:08:14.448 --> 00:08:16.158
not just here in HQ,

00:08:16.200 --> 00:08:17.701
but here in Geneva,

00:08:17.701 --> 00:08:21.455
in our six regional offices,
in our 152 country offices.

00:08:21.497 --> 00:08:23.666
People who are on the ground
every single day,

00:08:23.707 --> 00:08:26.585
they have a much harder job than I do.

00:08:26.961 --> 00:08:33.509
But we all have a role to play,
and I have felt overwhelmed at times.